// Findings ledger (docs/evaluation.md, "Findings"): every class of problem the corpus or code reading revealed, once,
// where it first showed. `testdetta-eval --summarize` writes findings.md from it: product classes per new repository,
// batch by batch, which tells whether repository-by-repository work converges.
// Add a batch when repositories join eval/corpus.json, and a finding when a fix closes a new class (kind: miss, a
// selection that left out a failing class; narrowing, a rule that could have left one out, found before it did;
// recording, a map that could not be recorded or was wrong; analysis, a hang or crash of the analysis; precision, a
// selection far wider than needed; evaluation, an artefact of the evaluator). The same class in another repository
// goes into seenAgain. A class that only a new TestDetta feature's first measurement could expose names the feature
// ("feature"), and is counted apart; a batch lists the repositories that could not be evaluated yet ("notEvaluated").
